      "10\nU.S.MAIL\nCUBAN MAIL\nGENERAL NEW\nTESTOR F-41),\nRATS INC.\nCOL. CHARLESA, LINDBERGHIN HAS",
      "POST-CARD\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS, INC.\nOFFICES:\nHAVANA\nSevilla Biltmore Arcade\nPhone A-2222\nKEY WEST\nLa Concha Hotel Bag.\nPhone 377\nLeave Key West 8.00 a.m. Leave Havana 3.45 p. m1.\nArrive Havana 9.15 a.M. Arrive Key West 5.15 p.m.\nCapote y Dier i Barnet 68) Habana\nOn Feb., 12th 1928, Col, Charies A.\nLindbergh acted as pilot on the Pan\nAmerican Airways Fokker planes, carry-\ning most of the delegates of the Sixth Pan\nAmerican Conference for rides over\nHavana.\nThe \"GENEFAL NEW\"-Fokker trimotor:\nWright \"Whirlwind u 5\" motors; eight\npassengers. pilot, and flight mechanic.\n2022.12"
